92186045417] [17592186066525 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066525 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9919e2c-cbe1-5c41-a1b1-57be787bd108" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066526 #edb/ref 1080 "4y\\sqrt{2y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ab5aca2-34cf-511d-b92f-1e7702541d5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066527 #edb/ref 1080 "8y\\sqrt{2y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066527 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066527 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64285070-c3b5-5963-aa25-3bf6449987b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068432 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068432 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{8z^3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068432 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a474788c-5b2b-570d-84bf-2c9575ac4f54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068432 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $8z^3$ as the product $4z^2 \\cdot 2z$ which contains a perfect square $(4z^2){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{8z^3}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{4z^2 \\cdot 2z}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{4z^2 \\cdot 2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2\\cdot 2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        |2z|\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        |2|\\cdot|z|\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n\t2|z|\\sqrt{2z}&\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068469 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1363" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068469 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{18y^3}$ given that $y \\geq 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068469 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "969be012-a830-564e-a355-00a4f1985ae8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068469 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $18y^3$ as the product $9y^2\\cdot 2y$ which contains a perfect square $(9y^2).$ Then, we separate the product into two separate radicals, one of which can be simplified:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sqrt{18y^3} &= \\\n\t\t\\sqrt{9y^2 \\cdot 2y} &= \\\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\\sqrt{9y^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\t\t\n\t\t\\sqrt{(3y)^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\t\t\n\t\t|3y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\t\t\n\t\t|3| \\cdot |y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\n\t\t3 \\cdot |y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y}\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince $y \\geq 0,$ we have $|y|=y,$ and we can simplify further. Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3 \\cdot |y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\n\t\t3 \\cdot y \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\n\t\t3y\\sqrt{2y}. &\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068676 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9980" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068676 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{50u^7}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068676 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce2e3248-96e3-5d69-9a16-1a62e0ce0eeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068676 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $50u^7$ as the product $25u^6\\cdot 2u$ which contains a perfect square $(25u^6){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{50u^7}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{25u^6\\cdot 2u}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{25u^6\\cdot 2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2\\cdot 2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t|5u^3|\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t|5|\\cdot |u^3|\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t5|u|^3 \\sqrt{2u}\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068826 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068826 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068826 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068826 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068826 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17