86045417] [17592186069762 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a8b2793-a5c0-588d-81b2-ae26ae1802aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069762 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069764 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069764 #edb/ref 1061 37757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069764 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "444844cf-a75f-58b6-bbc1-b9439090e46c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069764 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069800 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069800 #edb/ref 1061 4304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069800 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bfc154dc-32b4-5e94-a701-30a255009a40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069800 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069801 #edb/ref 1061 4311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069801 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16267a67-a93b-562b-88e6-0963346b1bfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069801 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069943 #edb/ref 1064 "The **product rule for radicals** states that the square root of a product equals the product of the square roots:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sqrt{ab} &=\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b}\n\t}\n$$\n\nWe can use the product rule to rewrite the square roots of algebraic expressions.\n\nAs an example, let's suppose we want to simplify the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{32y}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite $32y$ as the product $16 \\cdot 2y,$ which contains a perfect square $(16){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{32y}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 2y}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\\sqrt{4^2 \\cdot 2y}&\n\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n        \\sqrt{4^2\\cdot 2y}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{4^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2y}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n        \\sqrt{4^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2y}&=\\[3p