#edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501121 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501121 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501121 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501121 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501121 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7cd740e-2e2f-5d86-98a0-50d1b58bfb81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501139 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501139 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501139 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501139 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{25{r}^{3}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501139 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0902afad-f2ba-5dbf-8fa2-d595df73885c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501139 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $25{r}^{3}$ as the product $25{r}^{2}\\cdot r$ which contains a perfect square $(25{r}^{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{25{r}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{25{r}^{2}\\cdot r} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{25{r}^{2}\\cdot r} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(5r)^{2}\\cdot r} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(5r)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{r} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(5r)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{r} & = \\\\ |5r|\\cdot \\sqrt{r} & = \\\\ |5|\\cdot |r|\\cdot \\sqrt{r} & = \\\\ 5|r|\\sqrt{r} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501143 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501143 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501143 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501143 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{8{a}^{2}}$ given that $a\\ge 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501143 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1704928a-5b6a-5e32-992c-5da9fe38c678" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501143 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $8{a}^{2}$ as the product $4{a}^{2}\\cdot 2$ which contains a perfect square $(4{a}^{2}).$ Then, we can separate the product into two separate radicals, one of which can be simplified:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8{a}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4{a}^{2}\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(2a)^{2}\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(2a)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ |2a|\\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ |2|\\cdot |a|\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2\\cdot |a|\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $a\\ge 0,$ we have $|a|=a,$ and we can simplify further. Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |a|\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2\\cdot a\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2a\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501215 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501215 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142029" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501215 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501215 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{144{b}^{7}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501215 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b653142d-595d-5dac-942f-8b41a4d42831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501215 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $144{b}^{7}$ as the product $144{b}^{6}\\cdot b$ which contains a perfect square $(144{b}^{6}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{144{b}^{7}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{144{b}^{6}\\cdot b} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{144{b}^{6}\\cdot b} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(12{b}^{3})}^{2}\\cdot b} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(12{b}^{3})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{b} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(12{b}^{3})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{b} & = \\\\ |12{b}^{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{b} & = \\\\ |12|\\cdot |{b}^{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{b} & = \\\\ 12|b{|}^{3}\\sqrt{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501216 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501216 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141464" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501216 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501216 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{54{y}^{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501216 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b89f2670-8d2c-52b5-b612-dd1804214943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501216 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $54{y}^{2}$ as the product $9{y}^{2}\\cdot 6$ which contains a perfect square $(9{y}^{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{54{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9{y}^{2}\\cdot 6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{9{y}^{2}\\cdot 6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(3y)^{2}\\cdot 6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(3y)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(3y)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ |3y|\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ |3|\\cdot |y|\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 3|y|\\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501222 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501222 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141477" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501222 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501222 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{44{u}^{8}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501222 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2d5742a-0261-5618-8222-f4f0f769fb79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501222 #edb/ref 1074 "We first write $44{u}^{8}$ as the product $4{u}^{8}\\cdot 11$ which contains a perfect square $(4{u}^{8}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{44{u}^{8}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4{u}^{8}\\cdot 11} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4{u}^{8}\\cdot 11} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(2{u}^{4})}^{2}\\cdot 11} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(2{u}^{4})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(2{u}^{4})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & = \\\\ |2{u}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & = \\\\ |2|\\cdot |{u}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & = \\\\ 2|u{|}^{4}\\sqrt{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
